      "provider_message_id": null,
      "content": {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "A **runbook** is a step-by-step guide for operating or fixing a system—usually written so someone can follow it under pressure.\n\nIt typically covers:\n- When to use it (symptoms, alerts, triggers)\n- Exact actions to take (commands, checks, rollbacks)\n- Expected outcomes and what to do if something fails\n- Who to escalate to\n\nCommon uses: incident response, deployments, on-call handoffs, and recurring ops tasks. Unlike docs that explain *why*, a runbook focuses on *what to do next*.",
        "parts": null
      },
      "parent_id": "ed24fecc-29f7-5af2-a106-fc754fbb2dd5",
